A||||4||TheFiero64||Anyone ever play with VDG Generators?||||5||
Z||000000||TheFiero64||04-27-2001||03:43 PM||||My new hobby is Van De Graaf Generators. I got hooked after seeing the worlds biggest one at <A HREF="http://www.mos.org/sln/toe/toe.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.mos.org/sln/toe/toe.html</A> <P>Here is a cool site all about them <A HREF="http://www.amasci.com/emotor/vdg.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.amasci.com/emotor/vdg.html</A> <P>I've even started my own forum <A HREF="http://novogate.com/board/527/" TARGET=_blank>http://novogate.com/board/527/</A> <P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||5
Z||000001||DaRkLoRD||04-27-2001||04:18 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by TheFiero64:<BR><B>Here is a cool site all about them <A HREF="http://www.amasci.com/emotor/vdg.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.amasci.com/emotor/vdg.html</A> <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Cool, someone else knows about Bill Beatty's site.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I've seen plans for a simple electrostatic generator made with an old record and some fake fur from a craft store (as well as several other parts) it was operated with a hand crank, but I'd probably use an electric motor so I could build up a much bigger charge.. for which I need a nice big leyden jar.. I might try a VDG someday as well, but I have no plans for one in the near future. one of the hobby projects I want to undertake this summer that I'm really looking forward to is building my own rock tumbler. I had one when I was younger and it was pretty cool, so I'm gonna try and make a bigger one that can hold more rocks. the old one was something from the sears christmas catalog, and was pretty wimpy.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
Z||000002||TheFiero64||04-27-2001||04:28 PM||||I was going to build my own VDG, but I decided to get one on ebay. It should come in soon. I may build my own someday. I am going to try to make my own leyden jar and the soda bottle motor.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||04-27-2001||08:07 PM||||Be Extremely Careful With Leyden Jars.<P>The charges they can build can be lethal. Make sure you keep them shunted when you aren't using them or when you are transporting them.<P>Basic jars are easy to make. Can be allot of fun used carefully.<P>Trivia....<P>Recent research on the Arc of the Covenant indicates it may have been a very large Leydan jar in nature. This could easily explain why people who didn't treat it right had very short lifespans.||||reg||1
Z||000004||DaRkLoRD||04-28-2001||04:42 AM||||there was a documentary on TLC a couple of years ago about that, and I have a book on it as well. <BR>a leyden jar is an insulated container with metal layers on the inside and outside, with 2 discharge terminals on top. the ark of the covenent was a wooden box (insulator) lined inside and out with gold. there were 2 gold figures on top... makes perfect sense..   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>   <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>   <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A><p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 04-28-2001).]||||reg||3
